    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0142" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/52<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >3/16</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cousins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-15T11:00:00-06:00">July 15, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Referring to the Department’s strictly confidential circular telegram of July
                    11, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="82" xml:id="d165-f1"/> I informed President Carías of the
                    contents thereof and he will be very pleased to have the proposed <pb
                        facs="0143" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/> staff conversations take place at the
                    pleasure of the United States Government. His attitude is one of complete
                    cooperation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cousins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
